IMPORT prelude

-- Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004 (Singapore) -- who may see an individual's residential address on the
-- register (ss 30C, 30D, Sixth Schedule paras 2 to 4), who may call themselves "Chartered Accountant of Singapore" and how
-- registration as one is kept, suspended and appealed (ss 35B to 35I), and the Part 7 offences: ACRA's symbol and name, false
-- statements, obstruction, secrecy, and composition (ss 36, 37, 38, 39(6), 42, 44).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ACRAA2004.txt, with amendments
-- to Act 24 of 2025 (in force 6 May 2026) shown. THE ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS IN THE DEPOSIT IS OUT OF STEP WITH THE BODY for Part 7:
-- this encoding follows the BODY (36 symbol, 37 name, 38 false statements, 39 enforcement, 40 bodies corporate, 42 secrecy, 44
-- composition).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 9 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the provisions a company officer,
-- accountant or member of the public actually meets. Not encoded: the Authority's constitution, functions, finances and the
-- transfers of staff and property (Parts 2 to 6AA); the electronic transaction system mechanics (ss 27 to 30B) beyond s 30C/30D;
-- designated-entity designation and deletion (ss 35K, 35L); bodies corporate and partnership liability (s 40); service (s 42A); and
-- anything left to regulations ("prescribed" accounting services, proportions, compoundable offences).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004 -- conduct`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `30C, 30D and Sixth Schedule -- residential addresses`

-- s 30C(1): "Subject to subsection (2) and any exception specified in the Sixth Schedule, an individual's residential address must be
-- excluded from public disclosure." (2): the Registrar may end the exclusion under s 30D. (3): the exclusion "must" resume if the
-- Registrar receives notice of a contact address, or the Court so directs on appeal.
-- Sixth Schedule para 3(2): an address "filed or lodged ... before 9 December 2024 ... may be disclosed under section 30B(1)".
-- para 3(3): s 30C(1) "does not exclude an individual's contact address which is the same as his or her residential address".
GIVEN `filed before 9 December 2024` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the contact address is the residential address` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Registrar has ceased the exclusion` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the exclusion has resumed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the residential address may be publicly disclosed` IF
        `filed before 9 December 2024`
    OR  `the contact address is the residential address`
    OR  (`the Registrar has ceased the exclusion` AND (NOT `the exclusion has resumed`))

-- s 30D(1): the grounds are either that (a) communications sent to the contact address "requiring a response within a specified
-- period remain unanswered"; or (b) there is evidence that service at the contact address "is not effective to bring it to the
-- notice of the individual". (2)-(5): notice, a period for representations, and notice of the decision come first.
GIVEN `communications to the contact address went unanswered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `service at the contact address is shown to be ineffective` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `notice and a chance to make representations were given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may cease the exclusion` IF
        (`communications to the contact address went unanswered` OR `service at the contact address is shown to be ineffective`)
    AND `notice and a chance to make representations were given`

-- s 30D(7): appeal to the Court "within 30 days after the date of receiving the notice under subsection (5)".
GIVEN `days since the notice of decision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal against cessation is in time` IF
    `days since the notice of decision` AT MOST 30

-- s 30D(8): "The individual is not allowed to provide a contact address within 3 years after" the exclusion ceases, "unless the
-- Registrar is satisfied that there is good cause". Measured here in months (36).
GIVEN `months since the exclusion ceased` IS A NUMBER, `the Registrar is satisfied of good cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual may provide a new contact address` IF
        `months since the exclusion ceased` AT LEAST 36
    OR  `the Registrar is satisfied of good cause`

-- Sixth Schedule para 3(1): as an exception to s 30C(1), the residential address may go (a) to an authorised information service
-- provider -- who "must not disclose" it in any information service; (b) under s 30B(1)(b), i.e. to the para 4 persons: (a) a
-- trustee in bankruptcy, liquidator, judicial manager or receiver; (b) for anti-money-laundering purposes, a financial institution,
-- a licensed moneylender or a licensed estate agent; (c) to a Singapore law practice "to assist an advocate and solicitor ... in
-- effecting the service of process on the individual". Para 4A: it may be used "only" for that purpose.
DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `an authorised information service provider`
    `a liquidator`
    `a trustee in bankruptcy`
    `a bank checking for money laundering`
    `a licensed moneylender checking for money laundering`
    `a licensed estate agent checking for money laundering`
    `a law practice serving process`
    `a law practice researching a claim`
    `a journalist`
    `a member of the public`

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a protected residential address may be given to` IF
    CONSIDER `the recipient`
    WHEN `a law practice researching a claim` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a journalist` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a member of the public` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Sixth Schedule para 2(c): the Registrar or the Authority "must not" provide under s 30B(1) "a document filed or lodged ... on or
-- after 9 December 2024 that contains" an individual's date of birth, email address or mobile telephone number.
GIVEN `filed on or after 9 December 2024` IS A BOOLEAN, `it shows a date of birth, email or mobile number` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the document may be provided from the register` IF
    NOT (`filed on or after 9 December 2024` AND `it shows a date of birth, email or mobile number`)

§§ `35A, 35B -- the title "Chartered Accountant of Singapore"`

-- s 35A(1): "accounting entity" means "a public accountant, an accounting corporation, an accounting firm or an accounting limited
-- liability partnership". (2): a person "registered as a chartered accountant" is one registered by a designated entity "and whose
-- registration is not suspended".
-- s 35B(1): an accounting entity or a registered chartered accountant MAY use "Chartered Accountant of Singapore" and "CA
-- (Singapore)". (2): so may an approved entity.
-- s 35B(3): "An individual who is not registered as a chartered accountant, or whose registration as such is suspended ... must not"
-- hold out or use the expression. (4): a non-individual that is not an accounting entity or approved entity "must not".
--
-- A public accountant is an individual and an accounting entity. If not registered as a chartered accountant, s 35B(1) permits the
-- title and s 35B(3) forbids it. The text does not say which prevails; both are encoded as written.
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an accounting entity` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a registered chartered accountant not suspended` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an approved entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35B(1) or (2) permits the title` IF
        `is an accounting entity`
    OR  `is a registered chartered accountant not suspended`
    OR  `is an approved entity`

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an accounting entity` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a registered chartered accountant not suspended` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an approved entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35B(3) or (4) forbids the title` IF
    IF `is an individual`
    THEN NOT `is a registered chartered accountant not suspended`
    ELSE (NOT `is an accounting entity`) AND (NOT `is an approved entity`)

-- s 35B(5): (a) an individual (subsection (3)) -- fine up to $5,000; second or subsequent offence up to $10,000 or 6 months or both.
-- (b) a non-individual (subsection (4)) -- $5,000; second or subsequent $10,000 (no imprisonment).
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a repeat offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for misusing the title` MEANS
    IF `is a repeat offence` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a repeat offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment for misusing the title` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` AND `is a repeat offence` THEN 6 ELSE 0

§§ `35C -- approved entities`

-- s 35C(2)(b): (i) a company -- its constitution provides that at least two-thirds of the directors "(including the chairperson)" must
-- be chartered accountants, or if it has only one director, that director, or if only 2 directors, at least one; (ii), (iii) a
-- firm or LLP -- at least two-thirds of the partners, or if only 2 partners, at least one. "Any other prescribed proportion" is not
-- modelled. For a company the test is what the CONSTITUTION provides; here the numbers stand for that provision.
-- INFERENCE: "(including the chairperson)" is read as requiring the chairperson to be a chartered accountant under the two-thirds
-- limb. It could instead mean only that the chairperson counts among the directors.
DECLARE Entity IS ONE OF
    `a company`
    `a firm`
    `a limited liability partnership`

GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity, `members` IS A NUMBER, `chartered accountants` IS A NUMBER,
      `the chairperson is a chartered accountant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the composition condition is met` IF
    IF `members` EQUALS 2
    THEN `chartered accountants` AT LEAST 1
    ELSE IF `members` EQUALS 1
         THEN `chartered accountants` AT LEAST 1
         ELSE `chartered accountants` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `members` TIMES 2
              AND (`the chairperson is a chartered accountant` OR (NOT (`the entity` EQUALS `a company`)))

§§ `35D, 35E -- registration and renewal`

-- s 35D(1): "No person, except a designated entity, may register, or renew the registration of, any person as a chartered
-- accountant." Third Schedule: the only designated entity is the Institute of Singapore Chartered Accountants.
-- (6): anyone else who holds itself out as a designated entity or "purports to register" commits an offence ($5,000; repeat
-- $10,000 or 6 months or both).
GIVEN `is a designated entity` IS A BOOLEAN, `purports to register a chartered accountant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `purporting to register is an offence` IF
    (NOT `is a designated entity`) AND `purports to register a chartered accountant`

-- s 35D(3): registration "is valid for one year" and may be renewed for the same period. (4): the designated entity "must not renew"
-- if the accountant (a) ceases to be a member, (b) does not satisfy the membership-rule requirements, or (c) any prescribed
-- requirement; (5) nor "while the chartered accountant's membership ... is suspended".
GIVEN `is still a member` IS A BOOLEAN, `meets the membership rules` IS A BOOLEAN, `membership is suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registration may be renewed` IF
    `is still a member` AND `meets the membership rules` AND (NOT `membership is suspended`)

-- s 35E(3): a suspension that follows a suspended membership lasts "the shorter of" (a) the membership suspension and (b) "the
-- period remaining of the validity of the registration". Days.
GIVEN `days of membership suspension` IS A NUMBER, `days of registration remaining` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days the registration is suspended` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `days of membership suspension` `days of registration remaining`

-- s 35F(4): a designated entity may suspend instead of revoking "for a period not exceeding 10 months". s 35G(4): the Authority may
-- suspend, or extend a suspension, for not more than 10 months "in the aggregate".
GIVEN `months of suspension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension is within the limit` IF
    `months of suspension` AT MOST 10

§§ `35C(5), 35H, 35I -- appeals`

-- s 35C(5): refusal of approval -- appeal to the Minister within 30 days, "whose decision is final".
-- s 35H(1): a designated entity's refusal to register or renew, or revocation or suspension -- appeal to the Authority within 30
-- days; (6) "the decision of the Authority is final".
-- s 35I(1): the Authority's revocation, suspension or extension under s 35G -- appeal to the Minister within 30 days; (6) final.
-- s 35H(5), 35I(5): an appeal does not suspend the decision unless otherwise directed.
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `the Authority refuses approval as an approved entity`
    `the Institute refuses registration`
    `the Institute refuses renewal`
    `the Institute revokes registration`
    `the Institute suspends registration`
    `the Authority revokes registration`
    `the Authority suspends registration`
    `the Authority extends a suspension`

DECLARE Forum IS ONE OF
    `the Authority`
    `the Minister`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A Forum
`the appeal lies to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `the Institute refuses registration` THEN `the Authority`
    WHEN `the Institute refuses renewal` THEN `the Authority`
    WHEN `the Institute revokes registration` THEN `the Authority`
    WHEN `the Institute suspends registration` THEN `the Authority`
    OTHERWISE `the Minister`

GIVEN `days after the decision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `days after the decision` AT MOST 30

GIVEN `the appellant asked for a stay and it was directed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision is on hold pending appeal` IF
    `the appellant asked for a stay and it was directed`

§§ `36, 37, 38, 39(6), 42, 44 -- offences and composition`

-- s 36(2): using ACRA's symbol without written permission, or one resembling it so as to deceive -- $10,000 or 6 months or both,
-- and $250 a day for a continuing offence. s 37(3): the same for using the name or acronym "ACRA" without written permission.
-- s 38: false statements or intentionally suppressing a material fact "in relation to any application under this Act" -- $50,000
-- or 2 years or both. s 39(6): obstructing an officer, wilfully misstating or refusing information without lawful excuse, or
-- failing to comply with a lawful demand -- $10,000 or 2 years or both. s 42(4): breach of secrecy -- $10,000 or 12 months or both.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `misusing the ACRA symbol`
    `misusing the ACRA name`
    `a false statement in an application`
    `obstructing an ACRA officer`
    `breaching ACRA secrecy`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `a false statement in an application` THEN 50000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum months of imprisonment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misusing the ACRA symbol` THEN 6
    WHEN `misusing the ACRA name` THEN 6
    WHEN `a false statement in an application` THEN 24
    WHEN `obstructing an ACRA officer` THEN 24
    OTHERWISE 12

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the further daily fine while it continues` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misusing the ACRA symbol` THEN 250
    WHEN `misusing the ACRA name` THEN 250
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 38: "(a) makes any false statement which the person knows to be false or does not believe to be true or which the person makes
-- recklessly; or (b) intentionally suppresses any material fact".
GIVEN `in an application under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the statement is false` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or did not believe it true or was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `intentionally suppressed a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a false statement offence is committed` IF
        `in an application under this Act`
    AND (   (`the statement is false` AND `knew or did not believe it true or was reckless`)
         OR `intentionally suppressed a material fact`)

-- s 42(1): a present or former member, officer, employee, consultant or agent of the Authority, or committee member, "must not
-- disclose" information obtained in their duties unless (c) with permission; (d) for administering the Act or a Second Schedule law;
-- (e) as a court or written law requires or allows; (f) with the Authority's prior authorisation; (g) to assist investigation or
-- prosecution of any offence; (h) to assist another public officer to administer a written law; (i) in civil proceedings to which
-- the Authority is a party; (j) for disciplinary proceedings; (k) to a foreign audit regulator under s 59B of the Accountants Act.
-- (2): never for personal benefit.
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `with the permission of the person it came from`
    `to administer the Companies Act`
    `under a court order`
    `with the Authority's prior authorisation`
    `to help the police investigate an offence`
    `in civil proceedings the Authority is a party to`
    `for disciplinary proceedings`
    `to a foreign audit regulator under an arrangement`
    `to a friend over dinner`
    `to a business contact for a fee`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an ACRA insider may disclose` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `to a friend over dinner` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `to a business contact for a fee` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 44(1): an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a) one half
-- of the maximum fine and (b) $5,000. (Which offences are prescribed is left to regulations and not modelled.)
GIVEN `maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`maximum fine for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
